{"id": "q01", "type": "why", "question": "Revenue and operating income both increased in FY2025. Why did net income decrease?", "answer": "The provision for income taxes rose by $1,298M ($975M to $2,273M; effective tax rate 12.0% to 24.5%), which more than offset the increases in operating income (+$422M) and interest and other income (+$719M). Two items drove the tax increase: a $659M remeasurement of deferred tax assets from new tax incentive agreements in Singapore, and a $407M valuation allowance against corporate alternative minimum tax (CAMT) credits that are no longer expected to be realized after the One Big Beautiful Bill Act. Both are tax events, not changes in operating performance.", "evidence": [{"page": 30, "section": "MD&A > Results of Operations", "quote": "Net income $ 6,998 $ 7,177 $ (179)"}, {"page": 32, "section": "MD&A > Income Taxes", "quote": "$659 million remeasurement of deferred tax assets"}, {"page": 32, "section": "MD&A > Income Taxes", "quote": "$407 million valuation allowance against deferred tax assets"}, {"page": 47, "section": "Consolidated Statements of Operations", "quote": "Provision for income taxes 2,273 975"}], "numbers": {"operating_income_2025": 8289, "operating_income_2024": 7867, "other_income_2025": 1251, "other_income_2024": 532, "income_tax_2025": 2273, "income_tax_2024": 975, "net_income_2025": 6998, "net_income_2024": 7177, "etr_pct_2025": 24.5, "etr_pct_2024": 12.0, "singapore_dta_remeasurement": 659, "camt_valuation_allowance": 407}}
{"id": "q02", "type": "why", "question": "Why did the operating margin of Applied Global Services (AGS) decline?", "answer": "AGS operating margin fell 1.0 point, from 29.1% to 28.1%. The main causes were lower 200mm equipment revenue, higher headcount-related expenses to support business growth, and higher excess and obsolete inventory charges, partially offset by higher revenue from services and spares. Revenue grew from $6,225M to $6,385M, but operating income declined from $1,812M to $1,792M.", "evidence": [{"page": 32, "section": "MD&A > Segment Operating Income", "quote": "primarily due to a decrease in 200mm equipment net revenue"}], "numbers": {"ags_margin_pct_2025": 28.1, "ags_margin_pct_2024": 29.1, "ags_revenue_2025": 6385, "ags_revenue_2024": 6225, "ags_operating_income_2025": 1792, "ags_operating_income_2024": 1812}}
{"id": "q03", "type": "why", "question": "Net income decreased, so why did diluted EPS increase?", "answer": "Share repurchases reduced diluted weighted-average shares from 834M to 808M (about -3.1%), a larger decline than net income (about -2.5%), so diluted EPS rose from $8.61 to $8.66. FY2025 share repurchases totaled $4,895M. The report does not state this explanation; it is inferred from the income statement and cash flow statement.", "evidence": [{"page": 47, "section": "Consolidated Statements of Operations", "quote": "Diluted 808 834 845"}, {"page": 51, "section": "Consolidated Statements of Cash Flows", "quote": "Common stock repurchases (4,895) (3,823) (2,189)"}], "numbers": {"diluted_shares_m_2025": 808, "diluted_shares_m_2024": 834, "diluted_eps_2025": 8.66, "diluted_eps_2024": 8.61, "stock_repurchases_2025": 4895}}
{"id": "q04", "type": "why", "question": "Why did interest and other income increase sharply, and is the increase likely to recur?", "answer": "Interest and other income rose by $719M, from $532M to $1,251M, driven mainly by higher net gains on equity investments, partially offset by lower interest income from lower cash balances and lower market interest rates. The cash flow statement shows investment gains jumping from $15M to $792M. Because equity investment gains depend on market conditions, the increase should not be treated as recurring (this judgment is an inference, not a statement in the report).", "evidence": [{"page": 32, "section": "MD&A > Interest and Other Income", "quote": "higher net gain on equity investments"}, {"page": 51, "section": "Consolidated Statements of Cash Flows", "quote": "(Gain) loss and impairments on investments, net (792) (15)"}], "numbers": {"other_income_2025": 1251, "other_income_2024": 532, "investment_gain_2025": 792, "investment_gain_2024": 15}}
{"id": "q05", "type": "numeric", "question": "What was the FY2025 gross margin?", "answer": "48.7%. Verified against the income statement: gross profit of $13,808M divided by net revenue of $28,368M equals 48.67%.", "evidence": [{"page": 30, "section": "MD&A > Results of Operations", "quote": "Gross margin 48.7 % 47.5 %"}, {"page": 47, "section": "Consolidated Statements of Operations", "quote": "Gross profit 13,808 12,897"}], "numbers": {"gross_margin_pct_2025": 48.7, "gross_margin_pct_2024": 47.5, "gross_profit_2025": 13808, "revenue_2025": 28368}}
{"id": "q06", "type": "numeric", "question": "What were the effective tax rates for FY2025 and FY2024?", "answer": "24.5% in FY2025 and 12.0% in FY2024, an increase of 12.5 points.", "evidence": [{"page": 32, "section": "MD&A > Income Taxes", "quote": "Effective income tax rate 24.5 % 12.0 %"}], "numbers": {"etr_pct_2025": 24.5, "etr_pct_2024": 12.0}}
{"id": "q07", "type": "numeric", "question": "How much were FY2025 restructuring charges, and what share of the workforce is affected?", "answer": "Restructuring charges were $181M ($154M severance and other employee-related charges, $27M asset impairments), and about 4% of the global workforce is expected to be affected. The plan was approved in Q4 FY2025, is a one-time charge, and is expected to be completed in FY2026.", "evidence": [{"page": 31, "section": "MD&A > Operating Expenses", "quote": "approximately 4% of our global workforce"}, {"page": 70, "section": "Note 10 Restructuring Charges", "quote": "Severance and other employee-related charges $ 154"}], "numbers": {"restructuring_2025": 181, "severance_2025": 154, "asset_impairments_2025": 27, "workforce_pct": 4}}
{"id": "q08", "type": "compare", "question": "Which regions had the largest revenue increase and decrease, and what reason does the report give?", "answer": "Taiwan had the largest increase both in percentage (+71%) and in dollars (+$2,847M). Europe had the largest percentage decline (-33%, -$481M), but China had the largest dollar decline (-16%, -$1,588M). The report attributes regional changes only to changes in investments in semiconductor equipment and gives no specific reasons. Page 29 discusses U.S. export restrictions on China, but the report does not directly link them to the decline in China revenue.", "evidence": [{"page": 31, "section": "MD&A > Net revenue by geographic region", "quote": "primarily reflected changes in investments in semiconductor equipment"}, {"page": 29, "section": "MD&A > Overview", "quote": "limited our ability to provide certain products and services to customers in China"}], "numbers": {"taiwan_2025": 6857, "taiwan_2024": 4010, "europe_2025": 962, "europe_2024": 1443, "china_2025": 8529, "china_2024": 10117}}
{"id": "q09", "type": "compare", "question": "How and why did the Semiconductor Systems revenue mix by market change?", "answer": "The mix shifted from 68% to 67% for foundry, logic and other, from 28% to 26% for DRAM, and from 4% to 7% for NAND. Applying these shares to segment revenue ($19,911M to $20,798M) gives approximate amounts: foundry and logic about $13.5B to $13.9B (up), DRAM about $5.6B to $5.4B (down), and NAND about $0.8B to $1.5B (nearly doubled). These amounts are approximate because the shares are rounded. The report attributes foundry and logic growth to investment in leading-edge technologies, and memory growth to NAND equipment upgrades.", "evidence": [{"page": 30, "section": "MD&A > Results of Operations", "quote": "Flash memory (NAND) 7 % 4 %"}, {"page": 30, "section": "MD&A > Results of Operations", "quote": "increased customer investments in NAND fabrication equipment upgrades"}], "numbers": {"semi_systems_revenue_2025": 20798, "semi_systems_revenue_2024": 19911, "foundry_logic_pct_2025": 67, "foundry_logic_pct_2024": 68, "dram_pct_2025": 26, "dram_pct_2024": 28, "nand_pct_2025": 7, "nand_pct_2024": 4}}
